{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>even upon an orphan</b> — this indicates that you are not compassionate; were you to cast a lot [for] a wall or its like upon an orphan, you would not care, and you would join together and rejoice in your friend." "<b>and you dig</b> — from ויכרו להם כרה. And it is possible that תכרו is from כי יכרה איש בור, and it is fitting to attach it to תפילו."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:00.585115666Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}